From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:05:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] utils/edid: The screen size field decides the physical size

determineScreenPhysicalSizeMm() took the first detailed timing's image size
whenever its aspect matched the mode's. A 13.3 inch full HD notebook panel
declares 29 x 17 cm in the screen size field and 344 x 193 mm in its first
detailed timing: KWin sized it as a 15.5 inch panel and its first scale was
100 %.

The screen size field is the one a source is meant to size text with (VESA
E-EDID Release A2, 3.6.2). When it can be a screen (at least 10 cm by 6 cm,
an aspect between 1.2 and 2.6, not the 160 x 90 mm placeholder) it decides;
the detailed timing's millimetres (3.10.2) are used when they say the same
screen, within the centimetre the field is rounded to. A field that cannot
be a screen leaves the choice as it was. This is the rule the edition's boot
menu sizes its text with.

A virtual output that is given an EDID and no physical size takes the
EDID's size, as a DRM connector does, so that the output configuration test
reads the whole chain from the EDID's bytes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
